A replacement in BC7 keeps the usual alpha

An image that replaces a texture (patch 0002's replacement_for) is read
as the GS's own texel, whose alpha is 128 for a full one. A PNG is
brought to that scale when the port reads it; a BC7 image is uploaded as
it is, so its alpha would have to be authored in the GS's scale. A new
TexInfo flag, TEX_INFO_STANDARD_ALPHA, set when the replacement's format
is BC7, makes the ubershader scale the sampled alpha as
floor((a * 128 + 127) / 255), the same integers the port gives a PNG, so
a .dds file authored with 255 opaque draws like its PNG twin. A texture
that is not replaced is sampled as before.

The shaders are precompiled: gs/shaders/slangmosh.hpp is the bank
Granite's slangmosh tool makes from slangmosh.json, so it is made again.
Only the ubershader's modules and the offsets after them change.

How the bank is made (the command is the one gs/slangmosh.sh holds), in a
copy of gs/shaders (the include path of slangmosh.json is relative to it):

    slangmosh slangmosh.json --namespace ParallelGS --output slangmosh.hpp \
        --output-interface slangmosh_iface.hpp -O --strip

The slangmosh tool is built from Granite at GRANITE_COMMIT of
tools/versions.txt (16e7395f6a4858c1783dbf6f521f90b9d5f82ac5) with the
submodules at the commits Granite records, fetched from their own
repositories (Release build, GRANITE_RENDERER off, GRANITE_TOOLS on,
GRANITE_VULKAN_SPIRV_CROSS on, GRANITE_SHADER_COMPILER_OPTIMIZE on):
glslang 8f79344bdb5c151b450462e35283a731c4a0f158 (Themaister/glslang),
SPIRV-Tools 556c7ca95c6a309278c6cee98129d573827a05b4 (Themaister),
SPIRV-Headers 00898b201b4153d7198c3e0134dbf953c83bbfd7 (KhronosGroup),
SPIRV-Cross 38681a30e09679191cc3957719eeee76024f6daf (KhronosGroup),
shaderc 42c364eb27982ecfc9e00e384df205730e65b90c (google), rapidjson
06d58b9e848c650114556a23294d0b6440078c61 (miloyip), stb
c9064e317699d2e495f36ba4f9ac037e88ee371a (nothings).

The check: the same command, run on the unpatched gs/shaders of the
pinned paraLLEl-GS commit (3a66c19), makes that commit's slangmosh.hpp
byte for byte (2,100,370 bytes); run on the shaders this patch makes, it
makes the slangmosh.hpp below byte for byte (2,095,172 bytes). The bank
is a binary file of a megabyte, so it is a git binary patch (git
format-patch --binary), its base85 lines cut at other lengths.

Applied by tools/setup.sh, tools/setup.ps1 and tools/pc/pgs_patches.py to
the pinned paraLLEl-GS commit (tools/versions.txt). paraLLEl-GS is
LGPL-3.0-or-later; this patch is published with the port under the same
license.

diff --git a/gs/gs_interface.cpp b/gs/gs_interface.cpp
index 7c76a66..30e55ff 100644
--- a/gs/gs_interface.cpp
+++ b/gs/gs_interface.cpp
@@ -1852,6 +1852,9 @@ void GSInterface::drawing_kick_update_state(FBFeedbackMode feedback_mode, const
 		if (tex_index < MaxTextures)
 		{
 			auto &info = render_pass.tex_infos[tex_index].info;
+			// A BC7 replacement is authored with the usual alpha (255 opaque); the shader scales it to the GS's.
+			if (render_pass.tex_infos[tex_index].view->get_format() == VK_FORMAT_BC7_UNORM_BLOCK)
+				info.flags |= TEX_INFO_STANDARD_ALPHA;
 			if (info.arrayed)
 			{
 				p.tex |= TEX_PER_SAMPLE_BIT;
diff --git a/gs/shaders/data_structures.h b/gs/shaders/data_structures.h
index 62882ab..1332f43 100644
--- a/gs/shaders/data_structures.h
+++ b/gs/shaders/data_structures.h
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@ struct TexInfo
 
 CONSTEXPR int TEX_INFO_FORCE_SAMPLE_MAPPING = 0x1;
 CONSTEXPR int TEX_INFO_LONG_TERM_REFERENCE = 0x2;
+CONSTEXPR int TEX_INFO_STANDARD_ALPHA = 0x4;
 
 CONSTEXPR int PGS_FB_SWIZZLE_WIDTH_LOG2 = 3;
 CONSTEXPR int PGS_FB_SWIZZLE_HEIGHT_LOG2 = 3;
diff --git a/gs/shaders/slangmosh.hpp b/gs/shaders/slangmosh.hpp
index 7c90cffe978524445ecba86d23022eb38f0c2a55..736b00ae9f09e5d422e0401c6e035d60d8710da9 100644
